Visualizing Data with Grafana
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure Grafana on a Linux system
Set up Prometheus as a data source for metrics visualization
Configure Jaeger as a data source for distributed tracing
Create comprehensive dashboards to visualize OpenTelemetry metrics and traces
Build custom panels and queries for monitoring application performance
Understand the integration between OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, Jaeger, and Grafana
Implement real-time monitoring and alerting capabilities
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with Docker and containerization concepts
Knowledge of OpenTelemetry fundamentals from previous labs
Understanding of metrics and distributed tracing concepts
Basic knowledge of YAML configuration files
Familiarity with web browsers and HTTP concepts
